From 23aad931ad86179fd8e1bdca28c4da8dea19f2d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:55:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] TEMPO: semi-Lagrangian sedimentation falls back to
 piecewise constant on a negative edge

semilagrangian_sedimentation reconstructs each arrival cell as linear
between the edge values qmi and qpi, with the PLM safeguard of Juang and
Hong (2010), eq. (A4): fall back to piecewise constant where either edge
value is negative. TEMPO tested qpi(k) > 0 where the paper, and Thompson's
copy of the scheme, test qpi(k) < 0. It therefore fell back to constant in
every cell with a positive upper edge, which is nearly all of them, and kept
the linear profile only where the upper edge is negative or zero; the
negative values were then raised to the floor by max(xr, limit), which
creates water. In a unit test of the routine alone (a rain layer with a
sharp top), each call created 3.0-3.5e-4 of the precipitation; with the test
corrected, or with no floor, it conserves to 1e-16.

This changes the scheme's behaviour, not only its water budget: with
semi_sedi_flag (sedi_semi = .true., as UFS runs TEMPO) rain and graupel
sedimentation go from effectively piecewise constant to piecewise linear, as
the scheme was published.

In TEMPO's 59-level test column with semi-Lagrangian sedimentation (closure
as in the previous commit, gfortran, 20 s x 180 / 60 s x 60): 3.3e-3 /
2.2e-3 before, 3.0e-8 / 4.4e-8 after, as with standard sedimentation (2.9e-8
/ 4.3e-8).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
---
 src/module_mp_tempo_main.F90 | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/module_mp_tempo_main.F90 b/src/module_mp_tempo_main.F90
index c679965..11bbef6 100644
--- a/src/module_mp_tempo_main.F90
+++ b/src/module_mp_tempo_main.F90
@@ -1690,7 +1690,8 @@ module module_mp_tempo_main
       else
         qpi(k)=qa(k)+0.5_wp*(dip+dim)*dza(k)
         qmi(k)=2._wp*qa(k)-qpi(k)
-        if(qpi(k) > 0._wp .or. qmi(k) < 0._wp) then
+        ! fall back to piecewise constant if either edge value is negative
+        if(qpi(k) < 0._wp .or. qmi(k) < 0._wp) then
           qpi(k) = qa(k)
           qmi(k) = qa(k)
         endif
